  "transform": "return the marker-sized hidden region; each marker pixel is recovered from its horizontal, vertical, or 180-degree mirror orbit using virtual coordinate shape+1-index, and cropped-edge orbits use the transposed upper-left representative",
  "grid_shape": "output height and width equal the solid marker rectangle"
}
</annotation>
